ll out of your mouth': JD Vance fires back at El-Sayed over comments about Second Lady Usha Vance]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133662680.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/keep-my-wifes-name-the-hell-out-of-your-mouth-jd-vance-fires-back-at-el-sayed-over-comments-about-second-lady-usha-vance/articleshow/133662680.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/keep-my-wifes-name-the-hell-out-of-your-mouth-jd-vance-fires-back-at-el-sayed-over-comments-about-second-lady-usha-vance/articleshow/133662680.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T01:41:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133662683,imgsize-164046.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Built in 1743, this 1,050-acre Maryland farm became a War of 1812 battlefield where...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133662544.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable 1,050-acre estate in Chestertown, Maryland, dating back to 1743, is currently on the market. This site was pivotal during the Battle of Caulk's Field in the War of 1812, with remnants of history lying beneath the surface of the expansive farmland. The property boasts a charming colonial-style manor and a breathtaking historic landscape, now an intriguing opportunity in the high-end real estate sector.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/built-in-1743-this-1050-acre-maryland-farm-became-a-war-of-1812-battlefield-where-bullets-and-buckles-remained-buried-for-two-centuries-the-family-now-plans-to-sell/articleshow/133662544.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/built-in-1743-this-1050-acre-maryland-farm-became-a-war-of-1812-battlefield-where-bullets-and-buckles-remained-buried-for-two-centuries-the-family-now-plans-to-sell/articleshow/133662544.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T01:40:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133662684,imgsize-1836545.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At 19, Baylee Laine gave up scholarship and worked two jobs to take in her four younger siblings]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133662457.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At just twenty-one, Baylee Laine made the extraordinary decision to give up her college sports scholarship, dedicating herself instead to raising her four younger siblings. Working two jobs and sometimes sleeping in her legal office, she fought hard for custody. Her inspiring story of love and sacrifice recently captured the hearts of many on social media, where she now shares her life with her adopted siblings and her own daughter.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-19-baylee-laine-gave-up-a-full-softball-scholarship-and-worked-two-jobs-to-take-in-her-four-younger-siblings-after-a-two-year-fight-she-adopted-them/articleshow/133662457.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-19-baylee-laine-gave-up-a-full-softball-scholarship-and-worked-two-jobs-to-take-in-her-four-younger-siblings-after-a-two-year-fight-she-adopted-them/articleshow/133662457.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T01:13:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133662521,imgsize-1830903.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1781, a live oak stood beside one of Revolutionary War’s final major battles; 245 years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133660428.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Dedicated arborists are engaged in the meticulous restoration of a 300-year-old live oak tree located near the historic Eutaw Springs battlefield in South Carolina. The project involves the careful removal of outdated metal supports to enhance the tree’s longevity, while modern support systems and improved soil conditions are being implemented, all in preparation for the upcoming 250th anniversary of the United States.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1781-a-live-oak-stood-beside-one-of-the-revolutionary-wars-final-major-battles-245-years-later-crews-are-removing-old-chains-that-once-saved-it-but-are-now-choking-it/articleshow/133660428.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1781-a-live-oak-stood-beside-one-of-the-revolutionary-wars-final-major-battles-245-years-later-crews-are-removing-old-chains-that-once-saved-it-but-are-now-choking-it/articleshow/133660428.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T01:02:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133662447,imgsize-1583461.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don't come to the US, telling you with folded hands': Indian man's appeal to students goes viral; 'Feeling sad as I am making this video']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133662357.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/dont-come-to-the-us-telling-you-with-folded-hands-indian-mans-appeal-to-students-goes-viral-feeling-sad-as-i-am-making-this-vide