e-the-fact-that-i-was-in-a-wheelchair-and-dependent-on-others-for-powerful-words-on-disability-and-identity/articleshow/133660170.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-christopher-reeve-the-fact-that-i-was-in-a-wheelchair-and-dependent-on-others-for-powerful-words-on-disability-and-identity/articleshow/133660170.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-31T23:25:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133660328,imgsize-70646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1975, fewer than 800 Aleutian cackling geese remained; fox removal and habitat protection helped...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133659372.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Aleutian cackling goose, once on the brink of extinction, has experienced a significant revival. Thanks to targeted predator removal and the establishment of safeguarded wetlands, this nesting success story transitioned the geese from endangered to a regulated hunting classification. Now managed by the US Fish and Wildlife Service, this exemplifies the positive impact of wildlife management and habitat conservation efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1975-fewer-than-800-aleutian-cackling-geese-remained-fox-removal-and-habitat-protection-helped-the-population-rebound-to-around-200000-and-regulated-hunting-later-returned/articleshow/133659372.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1975-fewer-than-800-aleutian-cackling-geese-remained-fox-removal-and-habitat-protection-helped-the-population-rebound-to-around-200000-and-regulated-hunting-later-returned/articleshow/133659372.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-31T23:21:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133660215,imgsize-1295879.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US announces emergency executive shutdown of 110 driving schools for 5000 violations: 'No English, no trucking - it's common sense']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133660085.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-announces-emergency-executive-shutdown-of-110-driving-schools-for-5000-violations-no-english-no-trucking-its-common-sense/articleshow/133660085.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-announces-emergency-executive-shutdown-of-110-driving-schools-for-5000-violations-no-english-no-trucking-its-common-sense/articleshow/133660085.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-31T23:17:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133660172,imgsize-167270.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Vance says Trump’s dramatic Kharg Island post was meant as a signal to Iran]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133658179.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US Vice President JD Vance stated Donald Trump's social media post conveyed a message to Iran.  American military officials confirmed no strikes occurred on Kharg Island overnight.  An Iranian official dismissed Trump's post as laughable and not credible.  US forces did attack two Iranian launchers on Larak Island recently.  These developments renew security concerns in the Strait of Hormuz.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/jd-vance-says-donald-trumps-dramatic-kharg-island-post-was-meant-as-a-signal-to-iran/articleshow/133658179.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/jd-vance-says-donald-trumps-dramatic-kharg-island-post-was-meant-as-a-signal-to-iran/articleshow/133658179.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-31T22:17:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133658370,imgsize-112591.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Kohl’s closed in 2016 and sat vacant for nearly a decade; $28 million later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133657875.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An abandoned Kohl's store in Roswell, Georgia, has been redeveloped into a large church. This $28 million project created an 80,000-square-foot multi-use event venue. Eagles Nest Church purchased the site and completed the extensive renovations. The new facility will host worship services and various community events starting September 2026. Future development plans include additional retail and family-focused businesses on the property.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kohls-closed-in-2016-and-sat-vacant-for-nearly-a-decade-28-million-later-the-80000-square-foot-store-is-becoming-a-church-and-community-venue/articleshow/133657875.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-kohls-closed-in-2016-and-sat-vacant-for-nearly-a-decade-28-million-later-the-80000-square-foot-store-is-becoming-a-church-and-community-venue/articleshow/133657875.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-31T22:07:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133658310,imgsize-1700003.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[13 injured as shuttle bus crashes into barri