n-takeover-now-drives-uber-in-washington/articleshow/133654128.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-31T18:45:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133654252,imgsize-96915.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1,800 volunteers took turns pulling a 400-ton Japanese castle with ropes and...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133657471.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable achievement, thousands of volunteers in Japan successfully relocated a historic castle keep using age-old techniques. This monumental task represents a critical advancement in a decade-long restoration initiative. The keep has been repositioned closer to its original stone foundation, revealing archaeological treasures like ancient drainage systems and remnants of earlier walls. Visitors can anticipate the keep's full reopening by 2033.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/after-a-decade-long-restoration-1800-volunteers-took-turns-pulling-a-400-ton-japanese-castle-with-ropes-8000-people-had-applied-for-the-chance-to-help-move-it/articleshow/133657471.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/after-a-decade-long-restoration-1800-volunteers-took-turns-pulling-a-400-ton-japanese-castle-with-ropes-8000-people-had-applied-for-the-chance-to-help-move-it/articleshow/133657471.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-31T21:41:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133657839,imgsize-1824481.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Uncertainties’ rising: Xi calls for stronger cooperation in meeting with Putin]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" alig